  "full_text": "Hi, I'm Terry Davis. I'm going to give you a tour of my room. This is my Xeon 3GHz 12-24 core beast. It's called Black Satan, kind of like Black Sunshine. Anyway, here's my desk. There's Shasta. Everybody knows I drink the Shasta. Here's a bunch of old CD-ROMs with backups. Here's some wire wrap. These are a bunch of parts, resistors, capacitors, integrated circuits, nuts and bolts. I used to make wire wrap boards. And here's my old oscilloscope. These are my two old computers. This is a Core i7. And this is a Pentium D that runs native. We're actually seeing a native... This is a native install. I just rebooted. You're going to see it boot natively. The CIA broke the CD-ROM controller or some shit. I don't know what happened. It's really terrible. I can't get anything in or out because the CD-ROM won't work. I have to replace the controller. So I just did the bootloader. So this is a native install. That makes my morale good. I used to run it exclusively native. Now it runs in VMware, obviously. These are my parents books. I pay like $600 rent and these are parents books and stuff It's a room and board but mostly just I Used to eat more food now. It's no I pretty much buy my food. I walk to the store. I don't have a car Here's pretty much all my worldly possessions right here. I gave away all my stuff in 1996 when I was converted from atheism I didn't make a vow of poverty. I gave away my car kind of when I lost my license. And now I have a license. And when I went on disability, I realized that I didn't really want to... I couldn't afford a car. I would be painfully pinched if I had a car. I used to have a car. I gave it away to one of my siblings or nieces or something. Anyway... So, anyway, so that's my room.",
